{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "surface_forcing",
    "description": "PISM atmosphere/surface forcing component (stage 2 of the eqice project): the PIK atmosphere (atmosphere::PIK with the default 'martin' parameterization -- the Martin et al. (2011) eq. (1) mean-annual air temperature T_ma = 273.15 + 30 - 0.0075*usurf - 0.68775*lat*(-1), no seasonal variation T_ms = T_ma, and the time-independent precipitation field, prescribed by the Stage-1 driver as P(r) = (200 + 100 cos(pi r/Lx)) kg m^-2 yr^-1 since the real model reads it from a file), the PIK surface (surface::PIK: the SMB held constant -- the driver prescribes it as the atmosphere precipitation minus a deterministic Gaussian ablation blob -- partitioned with dummy_accumulation/dummy_melt/dummy_runoff (accumulation = max(smb,0), melt = runoff = max(-smb,0), so mass_flux = accumulation - runoff always) and the Martin 2011 surface temperature, field-for-field equal to the atmosphere air_temperature), and the coupled per-cell SurfaceOceanCoupler subassembly that wires the atmosphere + ocean + surface forcing maps for one cell (the Stage-2 coupling of the leaf components; the same equations as the leaf models, all through the shared template library). The yearly-cycle temperature time series is flat for the martin parameterization (T_ms = T_ma): the general YearlyCycle cosine formula T(t) = T_ma + (T_ms - T_ma) cos(2 pi (year_frac - summerday_frac)) is implemented and tested in its flat limit. All shared math is imported by reference from ./surface_forcing_templates.esm; the ocean side of the coupled model is in ./ocean_coupling.esm. Tests assert the instantaneous boundary outputs dumped by the instrumented PISM v2.3.2 run (stage1/dumps/surface_ocean/). Deferred: the Uniform/Given atmosphere models, the huybrechts_dewolde / era_interim / martin_huybrechts_dewolde parameterizations, the Anomaly / Delta_T / Delta_P / elevation_change / Frac_P precipitation modifiers, the PDD surface model (I), DEBM/ISMIP6/EISMINT/Simple/Given surfaces, ForceThickness, and sea-level coupling."
  },
  "models": {
    "AtmospherePIK": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "./surface_forcing_templates.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "usurf_m": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 1490.5051884649215,
          "description": "ice surface elevation (geometry.ice_surface_elevation); the dome cell (15,15) value"
        },
        "lat_deg": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "degrees",
          "default": -70.0,
          "description": "latitude in degrees north (geometry.latitude); the dome cell value"
        },
        "r_m": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "radius from the dome center max(|x|, |y|)-style radial distance (grid::radius); the prescribed precipitation field is radial"
        },
        "Lx_m": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 900000.0,
          "description": "domain half-width (grid.Lx = 900 km in the test-F run)"
        },
        "precip_scale": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "default": 3.1688764640818492e-06,
          "description": "100 kg m^-2 yr^-1 converted to kg m^-2 s^-1 with 1 year = 3.15569259747e7 s (the UDUNITS tropical year); the amplitude of the driver's prescribed precipitation field"
        },
        "year_frac": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "fraction of the year at which the temperature time series is sampled (the dump samples ts = {0..1 year}/12)"
        },
        "summerday_frac": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.5366302288352832,
          "description": "fraction of the year of the summer peak day (atmosphere.fausto_air_temp.summer_peak_day = 196 days / 365.24219 days); irrelevant for the martin parameterization, whose cycle amplitude is zero"
        },
        "T_ma": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "mean annual near-surface air temperature T_ma = 303.15 + 0.68775*lat - 0.0075*usurf (atmosphere::PIK air_temperature(); Martin et al. 2011 eq. (1))"
        },
        "T_ms": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "mean summer near-surface air temperature; for the martin parameterization T_ms = T_ma (no seasonal variation)"
        },
        "precipitation": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "description": "time-independent precipitation rate (atmosphere::PIK precipitation(); held constant in time; the driver prescribes it)"
        },
        "T_cycle": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "yearly-cycle near-surface air temperature at the sampled year_frac (atmosphere::YearlyCycle::temp_time_series): T_ma + (T_ms - T_ma) cos(2 pi (year_frac - summerday_frac)); flat for martin"
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "_comment": "atmosphere::PIK::martin2011_mean_annual: T_ma = 273.15 + 30 - 0.0075*usurf - 0.68775*lat*(-1) (Martin et al. 2011 eq. (1); the dump's air_temp_atm and T_ma_analytic).",
          "lhs": "T_ma",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "martin_mean_annual_temperature",
            "args": ["usurf_m", "lat_deg"]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "atmosphere::PIK::martin2011: T_ms = T_ma (no seasonal variation).",
          "lhs": "T_ms",
          "rhs": "T_ma"
        },
        {
          "_comment": "atmosphere::PIK precipitation: time-independent field, prescribed by the Stage-1 driver as P(r) = 100*(2 + cos(pi r/Lx)) kg m^-2 yr^-1 (converted to kg m^-2 s^-1); in real runs the model reads it from a file (atmosphere.pik.file).",
          "lhs": "precipitation",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "prescribed_precipitation",
            "args": ["r_m", "Lx_m"]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "atmosphere::YearlyCycle::temp_time_series_impl: T(t) = T_ma + (T_ms - T_ma) cos(2 pi (year_frac - summerday_frac)); flat for martin because T_ms = T_ma.",
          "lhs": "T_cycle",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "yearly_cycle_temperature",
            "args": ["T_ma", "T_ms", "year_frac", "summerday_frac"]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
    {
      "id": "tma_lat_m60_usurf_0",
      "description": "Martin 2011 mean-annual air temperature at lat=-60 deg, usurf=0 m: T_ma = 303.15 + 0.68775*lat - 0.0075*usurf, T_ms = T_ma (no seasonal cycle) (stage1/dumps/surface_ocean/atmosphere_temperature.csv).",
      "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 1.0 },
      "parameter_overrides": {"usurf_m":0.0,"lat_deg":-60.0},
      "assertions": [
        { "variable": "T_ma", "time": 0.0, "expected": 261.885, "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-12 } },
        { "variable": "T_ms", "time": 0.0, "expected": 261.885, "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-12 } }
      ]
    },
    {
